{"signature": "559c157387450bf4d0b9115c7e004766da0a83105d93cd24bbb3cc8c58a1c5ef", "result": {"checks": {"check": {"scope": {"id": "check", "service": "confluence", "file": "confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions", "field": "page_id", "values": ["page_economy_design", "page_liveops_calendar", "page_prod_home", "page_season_pass_spec", "page_zm3d_gdd"]}, "matches": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/37", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_economy_design", "record": {"id": "ver_economy_design_v1", "page_id": "page_economy_design", "number": 1, "title": "Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives & Boosters", "body": "<p>Cross-game reference for currencies, lives, and boosters.</p><h2>Currency model</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Unit</th><th>Equals</th></tr><tr><td>1 US dollar</td><td>1,000 coins</td></tr><tr><td>1 gem</td><td>10 coins</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Level victories pay out roughly 40 gold. The ZM3D Master Item List holds 251 items across 23 categories.</p><h2>Booster costs</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Booster</th><th>Coin cost</th></tr><tr><td>Catapult / Broom / Tornado / Taser</td><td>333</td></tr><tr><td>Glue</td><td>300</td></tr><tr><td>Trampoline</td><td>200</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Domino Delights coin rewards are tuned generously to keep the early loop rewarding; sink balance under review.</p>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0005", "message": "Pre-cut economy: baseline currency + booster tables before the April 2025 Domino Delights reward reduction.", "created_at": "2025-03-05T11:20:00Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/38", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_economy_design", "record": {"id": "ver_page_economy_design_v11", "page_id": "page_economy_design", "number": 2, "title": "Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives & Boosters", "body": "<p>This page is the cross-game reference for how our soft and hard currencies, lives, and boosters are priced and tuned. It is owned by Design and kept in sync with the individual game design docs \u2014 see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Domino Delights \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Domino Delights \u2014 Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link> and <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link> for the per-game economy layers built on top of these primitives.</p><h2>Currency model</h2><p>Every title uses the same currency model \u2014 soft coins, premium gems and bones so tuning intuition transfers between games. Coins are the soft currency earned in play; gems are the premium hard currency bought or awarded sparingly. The conversion is fixed across the studio:</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Unit</th><th>Equals</th><th>Notes</th></tr><tr><td>1 US dollar</td><td>1,000 coins</td><td>Reference peg for IAP sizing; not a direct store SKU.</td></tr><tr><td>1 gem</td><td>10 coins</td><td>Hard currency; used for premium sinks and gating.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Level victories pay out coins on a per-level band, which anchors the earn side of the loop against the booster sinks below.</p><h3>Zombie Match 3D item catalog</h3><p>The ZM3D Master Item List is the source of truth for tunable objects: it currently holds <strong>250</strong> items spread across 22 categories (boosters, tiles, cosmetics, packs, and event-only entitlements). When adding a category, register it here first so the balancing sheet and the client stay aligned.</p><h2>Booster costs</h2><p>Boosters are the primary sink. Prices are per game and are <em>not</em> shared across titles: Zombie Match 3D prices its in-run power tools in gems, while Domino Delights prices everything in coins.</p><h3>Zombie Match 3D</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Booster</th><th>Cost</th><th>Currency</th></tr><tr><td>Broom</td><td>10</td><td>Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Tornado</td><td>12</td><td>Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Catapult</td><td>15</td><td>Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Taser</td><td>20</td><td>Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Trampoline</td><td>1,500</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Glue</td><td>1,500</td><td>Coins</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Domino Delights</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Booster</th><th>Cost</th><th>Currency</th></tr><tr><td>Rewind</td><td>500</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Dynamite</td><td>1,000</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Draw 3</td><td>1,200</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Wildcard</td><td>1,600</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Draw 5</td><td>1,800</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Gust</td><td>2,000</td><td>Coins</td></tr></tbody></table><ul><li>Domino Delights prices entirely in coins on a much wider ladder; see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Domino Delights &mdash; Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Domino Delights &mdash; Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link> for the per-level earn curve these sit against.</li><li>The two games do <strong>not</strong> share a booster price band &mdash; only the currency model is shared.</li></ul><h2>The Domino Delights coin cut (April 2025)</h2><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"warning\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>In <strong>April 2025</strong> we cut Domino Delights coin rewards by roughly 50% to stop runaway coin inflation. The 99th-percentile daily earn fell from about 4,554 coins to about 2,262 coins. Do not revert reward payouts on GoD without re-running the sink analysis \u2014 the pre-cut curve was unrecoverable.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>The symptom was that high-engagement players accumulated coins faster than any sink could absorb, so boosters felt free and the difficulty curve flattened. After the cut, average booster spend nudged up as expected and the coin balance distribution stopped climbing. The changes were applied to the live economy tables under the \"Game of Dominoes\" (GoD) codename and mirrored into this page's tuning constants.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>Lives regeneration and refill pricing are game-specific and documented in each GDD. This page documents title-specific currency and booster primitives; only the soft-/hard-currency pattern is shared.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0005", "message": "Align leftover wiki claims to stack, ledger, and session stats", "created_at": "2025-05-06T10:32:36Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/39", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_economy_design", "record": {"id": "ver_0f588252f15aabefb69a2455f3378bf7", "page_id": "page_economy_design", "number": 3, "title": "Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives & Boosters", "body": "<p>This page is the cross-game reference for how our soft and hard currencies, lives, and boosters are priced and tuned. It is owned by Design and kept in sync with the individual game design docs - see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Domino Delights \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Domino Delights - Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link> and <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Zombie Match 3D - Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link> for the per-game economy layers built on top of these primitives.</p><h2>Currency model</h2><p>The currency model is per title. Zombie Match 3D uses coins, gems and bones; Domino Delights uses coins, gems and hero shards; Combo Fighter uses Silver, Gold, Experience, Gems and Tickets. Gems is the only currency common to all three by name; Combo Fighter's soft currencies are Silver and Gold rather than coins, so the shared primitive is the soft/hard pair, not the word \"coins\". Coins are the soft currency earned in play; gems are the premium hard currency bought or awarded sparingly. The conversion below is the Zombie Match 3D reference; Domino Delights adjusted its IAP payouts the same month (commit <code>ceb6021fb</code>, 9 April 2025):</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Unit</th><th>Equals</th><th>Notes</th></tr><tr><td>1 US dollar</td><td>1,000 coins</td><td>Reference peg for IAP sizing; not a direct store SKU.</td></tr><tr><td>1 gem</td><td>10 coins</td><td>Hard currency; used for premium sinks and gating.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Level victories pay out coins on a per-level band, which anchors the earn side of the loop against the booster sinks below.</p><h3>Zombie Match 3D item catalog</h3><p>The ZM3D Master Item List is the source of truth for tunable objects: it currently holds <strong>250</strong> items spread across 21 categories (boosters, tiles, cosmetics, packs, and event-only entitlements). When adding a category, register it here first so the balancing sheet and the client stay aligned.</p><h2>Booster costs</h2><p>Currency units and values are title-specific; only the general soft-/hard-currency pattern is shared. The retained source confirms these Zombie Match 3D per-unit coin values and does not support a 1,500-coin, 30-minute unlimited assignment.</p><h3>Zombie Match 3D</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Booster</th><th>Per-unit coin cost</th></tr><tr><td>Broom</td><td>10 Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Tornado</td><td>12 Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Catapult</td><td>15 Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Taser</td><td>20 Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Glue (pre-level, one use)</td><td>400 Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Trampoline (pre-level, one use)</td><td>200 Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Trampoline or Glue, rotating shop (30 minutes unlimited)</td><td>1,500 Coins</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Domino Delights</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Booster</th><th>Cost</th><th>Currency</th></tr><tr><td>Rewind</td><td>500</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Dynamite</td><td>1,000</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Draw 3</td><td>1,200</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Wildcard</td><td>1,600</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Draw 5 (out-of-moves continue only)</td><td>1,800</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Gust</td><td>2,000</td><td>Coins</td></tr></tbody></table><ul><li>Domino Delights' main shop prices in coins on a much wider ladder; see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Domino Delights &mdash; Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Domino Delights - Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link> for the per-level earn curve these sit against.</li><li>The daily rotating shop carries gem-priced equivalents of the same boosters &mdash; Rewind 50, Dynamite 100, Draw 3 120, Wildcard 160, Gust 200 Gems &mdash; so the shop is not coin-only even though every in-level charge above is. Draw 5 has no shop SKU at all; 1,800 Coins is strictly the out-of-moves continue price.</li><li>The two games do <strong>not</strong> share a booster price band - only the currency model is shared.</li></ul><h2>The Domino Delights coin cut (April 2025)</h2><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"warning\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>In <strong>April 2025</strong> we cut Domino Delights <em>first-time level-completion</em> coin rewards by 34.4% - the nine-cell star table fell from a 480-coin sum to 315 - to stop runaway coin inflation. A straight 50% cut was the preferred option on paper, but it is not what shipped. The star table was not the only faucet cut in the same window &mdash; on-board chest coins went 300 to 100, hourly collection 150 to 100, chapter rewards 1000 to 500, the 4-streak multiplier 80x to 40x, mini-game refresh 2h to 24h, and Lucky Drop's infinite-lives grant 1800s to 300s &mdash; which is why the p99 falls further than the star-table percentage alone would suggest. The 99th-percentile daily earn fell from about 25,000 coins to about 8,500. IAP payouts were re-tuned the same month (commit <code>ceb6021fb</code>, 9 April 2025); the size of that offset was never written down, so do not quote one. Do not revert reward payouts on GoD without re-running the sink analysis - the pre-cut curve is recoverable from commit <code>1ee438b6a6</code> and from the v2.0 economy workbook.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>The symptom was that high-engagement players accumulated coins faster than any sink could absorb, so boosters felt free and the difficulty curve flattened. After the cut, average booster spend nudged up as expected and the coin balance distribution stopped climbing. The changes were applied to the live economy tables under the \"Game of Dominoes\" (GoD) codename and mirrored into this page's tuning constants.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>Lives regeneration and refill pricing are game-specific and documented in each GDD. This page only fixes the shared currency and booster primitives.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0005", "message": null, "created_at": "2025-09-21T02:19:30Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/45", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_liveops_calendar", "record": {"id": "ver_9d84767e1fee452ba239f033ef6b8c42", "page_id": "page_liveops_calendar", "number": 1, "title": "Live-Ops Event Calendar & Planning", "body": "<p>Owner: Frederick Stone (Growth/UA, departed Oct 2025). This page is the single source of truth for what live-ops events are scheduled, on which game, and at what cadence. It pairs with the runtime that actually fires these events &mdash; for architecture, the scheduler's known fragility, and the July 2025 outage, see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Live-Ops Event Engine\"/><ac:link-body>Live-Ops Event Engine</ac:link-body></ac:link>. Event goals are set against the metrics bar tracked in <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Product OKRs &mdash; 2025 H1\"/><ac:link-body>Product OKRs &mdash; 2025 H1</ac:link-body></ac:link>.</p><h2>Event calendar</h2><p>Every timed event we have run or currently run across the portfolio. \"Cadence\" is how the slot recurs; \"status\" is where the event stands as of the latest planning review.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Event</th><th>Game</th><th>Cadence</th><th>Status</th></tr><tr><td>Nathan's Treasure Hunt</td><td>Domino Delights (\"Game of Dominoes\" / GoD)</td><td>One-off seasonal</td><td>Shipped Dec 2024</td></tr><tr><td>Win &amp; Collect</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring weekly</td><td>First shipped Oct 2024</td></tr><tr><td>River Rush</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring weekly</td><td>First shipped Apr-May 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Plague Race</td><td>Zombie Match 3D (\"Puzzles vs Zombies\")</td><td>Recurring</td><td>Live; algo bug Aug 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Zombie Lane</td><td>Zombie Match 3D</td><td>One-off seasonal</td><td>Shipped Jun 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Endless Monster Mode</td><td>Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Permanent mode with daily and weekly resets</td><td>Live</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Notes on individual events</h3><ul><li><strong>Nathan's Treasure Hunt</strong> &mdash; our best-performing GoD seasonal to date; the reward-ladder structure is the template we now reuse for one-off events.</li><li><strong>Plague Race</strong> &mdash; the recurring ranked competition on ZM3D. A scoring/matchmaking algorithm bug surfaced in Aug 2025 and skewed leaderboard settlement; treat pre-fix cohorts with caution when reading event revenue.</li><li><strong>Endless Monster Mode</strong> \u2014 a permanent board mode with daily and weekly reset behavior, not a seasonal event.</li></ul><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"warning\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>July 2025 scheduler outage.</strong> The event/lives scheduler stalled for roughly two weeks in July 2025, so scheduled events did not fire and the published calendar diverged from what players actually saw. Do not backfill or reason about that window from this calendar &mdash; the Live-Ops Event Engine page holds the reconstructed timeline and the revenue impact.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Planning cadence</h2><p>We are a ~16-person studio, so live-ops planning is deliberately lightweight &mdash; one recurring meeting and one shared calendar, not a dedicated ops team. The working rhythm:</p><ul><li><strong>Weekly slotting review (Mondays).</strong> Design, led by Julia Lawson, walks the next four weeks; Frederick Stone participated before his October 2025 departure: which recurring slots fire (Endless Monster Mode in its Aug/Nov seasons, Plague Race on its ranked cadence) and whether a one-off seasonal drops on top.</li><li><strong>Two-week content lock.</strong> Event config &mdash; reward tables, windows, cohort targeting &mdash; must be authored and reviewed at least two weeks before the window opens, so QA has a full sprint to validate on staging.</li><li><strong>No overlapping recurring competitions.</strong> We do not run two ranked events on the same game at once; it splits the leaderboard population and muddies the revenue read.</li><li><strong>Post-event read.</strong> Each event gets a short retro against its target from Product OKRs before the slot is reused.</li></ul><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>The recurring slots (Endless Monster Mode (Aug and Nov 2025 seasons); Plague Race ranked) are the backbone of the calendar. One-off seasonals like Nathan's Treasure Hunt are layered on for spikes &mdash; they are the exception, not the base cadence, and should never displace a recurring slot without documented Product approval.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0038", "message": "Imported", "created_at": "2025-11-01T13:52:39Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/46", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_liveops_calendar", "record": {"id": "ver_page_liveops_calendar_v12", "page_id": "page_liveops_calendar", "number": 2, "title": "Live-Ops Event Calendar & Planning", "body": "<p>Owner: Frederick Stone (Growth/UA, departed Oct 2025). This page is the single source of truth for what live-ops events are scheduled, on which game, and at what cadence. It pairs with the runtime that actually fires these events \u2014 for architecture, the scheduler's known fragility, and the July 2025 outage, see <ac:link><ri:page ri:space-key=\"ENG\" ri:content-title=\"Live-Ops Event Engine\"/><ac:link-body>Live-Ops Event Engine</ac:link-body></ac:link>. Event goals are set against the metrics bar tracked in <ac:link><ri:page ri:space-key=\"PROD\" ri:content-title=\"Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1\"/><ac:link-body>Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1</ac:link-body></ac:link>.</p><h2>Event calendar</h2><p>Named planning slots (a slot can ship more than once; status is the first-ship or latest planning note, not every historical run). \"Cadence\" is how the slot recurs; \"status\" is where the event stands as of the latest planning review.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Event</th><th>Game</th><th>Cadence</th><th>Status</th></tr><tr><td>Weekly Quests</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring</td><td>Failed Nov 2024 (ads-quest misdeploy)</td></tr><tr><td>Lucky Drop</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring seasonal</td><td>Shipped Oct 2024</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly Leaderboards</td><td>Domino Delights / Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Recurring</td><td>Live</td></tr><tr><td>Nathan's Treasure Hunt</td><td>Domino Delights (\"Game of Dominoes\" / GoD)</td><td>One-off seasonal</td><td>Shipped Dec 2024</td></tr><tr><td>Streak Fever</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>One-off seasonal</td><td>Shipped Dec 2024</td></tr><tr><td>Win &amp; Collect</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring weekly</td><td>First shipped Oct 2024</td></tr><tr><td>River Rush</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring weekly</td><td>First shipped Apr-May 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Plague Race</td><td>Zombie Match 3D (\"Puzzles vs Zombies\")</td><td>Recurring</td><td>Live; algo bug Aug 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Zombie Lane</td><td>Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Recurring seasonal</td><td>Shipped Jun 2025; re-run Jul 2025 (failed, scheduler outage) and Sep&#8211;Oct 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Endless Monster Mode</td><td>Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Permanent mode with daily and weekly resets</td><td>Live</td></tr><tr><td>Collect &amp; Win</td><td>Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Recurring</td><td>First shipped Sep 2025</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Notes on individual events</h3><ul><li><strong>Nathan's Treasure Hunt</strong> \u2014 our best-performing GoD seasonal to date; the reward-ladder structure is the template we now reuse for one-off events.</li><li><strong>Plague Race</strong> \u2014 the recurring ranked competition on ZM3D. A scoring/matchmaking algorithm bug surfaced in Aug 2025 and skewed leaderboard settlement; treat pre-fix cohorts with caution when reading event revenue.</li><li><strong>Endless Monster Mode</strong> \u2014 a permanent board mode with daily and weekly reset behavior, not a seasonal event.</li></ul><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"warning\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>July 2025 scheduler outage.</strong> The event/lives scheduler stalled for roughly two weeks in July 2025, so scheduled events did not fire and the published calendar diverged from what players actually saw. Do not backfill or reason about that window from this calendar \u2014 the Live-Ops Event Engine page holds the reconstructed timeline and the revenue impact.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Planning cadence</h2><p>We are a ~16-person studio, so live-ops planning is deliberately lightweight \u2014 one recurring meeting and one shared calendar, not a dedicated ops team. The working rhythm:</p><ul><li><strong>Weekly slotting review (Mondays).</strong> Design, led by Julia Lawson, walks the next four weeks; Frederick Stone participated before his October 2025 departure: which recurring slots fire (Endless Monster Mode in its Aug/Nov seasons, Plague Race on its ranked cadence) and whether a one-off seasonal drops on top.</li><li><strong>Two-week content lock.</strong> Event config \u2014 reward tables, windows, cohort targeting \u2014 must be authored and reviewed at least two weeks before the window opens, so QA has a full sprint to validate on staging.</li><li><strong>No overlapping recurring competitions.</strong> We do not run two ranked events on the same game at once; it splits the leaderboard population and muddies the revenue read.</li><li><strong>Post-event read.</strong> Each event gets a short retro against its target from Product OKRs before the slot is reused.</li></ul><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>The recurring slots (Endless Monster Mode (Aug and Nov 2025 seasons); Plague Race ranked) are the backbone of the calendar. One-off seasonals like Nathan's Treasure Hunt are layered on for spikes \u2014 they are the exception, not the base cadence, and should never displace a recurring slot without documented Product approval.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0038", "message": "Align wiki figures and event slots to the warehouse", "created_at": "2025-12-06T22:11:24Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/47", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_liveops_calendar", "record": {"id": "ver_284d8e5e40907aeec83e8b2fea40a166", "page_id": "page_liveops_calendar", "number": 3, "title": "Live-Ops Event Calendar & Planning", "body": "<p>Owner: Frederick Stone (Growth/UA, departed Oct 2025). This page is the single source of truth for what live-ops events are scheduled, on which game, and at what cadence. It pairs with the runtime that actually fires these events - for architecture, the scheduler's known fragility, and the July 2025 outage, see <ac:link><ri:page ri:space-key=\"ENG\" ri:content-title=\"Live-Ops Event Engine\"/><ac:link-body>Live-Ops Event Engine</ac:link-body></ac:link>. Event goals are set against the metrics bar tracked in <ac:link><ri:page ri:space-key=\"PROD\" ri:content-title=\"Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1\"/><ac:link-body>Product OKRs - 2025 H1</ac:link-body></ac:link>.</p><h2>Event calendar</h2><p>Named planning slots (a slot can ship more than once; status is the first-ship or latest planning note, not every historical run). \"Cadence\" is how the slot recurs; \"status\" is where the event stands as of the latest planning review.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Event</th><th>Game</th><th>Cadence</th><th>Status</th></tr><tr><td>Weekly Quests</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring</td><td>Failed Nov 2024 (ads-quest misdeploy)</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly Leaderboards</td><td>Domino Delights / Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Recurring</td><td>Live</td></tr><tr><td>Nathan's Treasure Hunt</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>One-off seasonal</td><td>Shipped Dec 2024</td></tr><tr><td>Axe Arena</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring weekly, 2-day windows (roughly three per week)</td><td>Shipped Feb 2025 &mdash; first-try / win-streak scoring; affected by the 2025 weekend scheduler outage from 15 May</td></tr><tr><td>Streak Fever</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring weekly</td><td>Shipped Apr 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Win &amp; Collect</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring weekly, in three staggered windows (Mon-Tue, Wed-Thu, Fri-Sun) that all players share</td><td>Shipped Oct 2024 &mdash; Domino Delights' first live event</td></tr><tr><td>River Rush</td><td>Domino Delights</td><td>Recurring weekly</td><td>Shipped Apr 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Plague Race</td><td>Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Recurring</td><td>Live; algo bug Aug 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Zombie Lane</td><td>Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Recurring seasonal</td><td>Shipped Jun 2025 and Sep-Oct 2025</td></tr><tr><td>Endless Monster Mode</td><td>Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Recurring - daily reset 00:00 UTC, weekly reset Monday 00:00 UTC</td><td>Live; also one of the three permanent board modes</td></tr><tr><td>Collect &amp; Win</td><td>Zombie Match 3D</td><td>Recurring weekly, in three staggered windows (Mon-Tue, Wed-Thu, Fri-Sun) that all players share</td><td>Shipped Sep 2025. Same feature as Win &amp; Collect on Domino Delights, under a different name</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Notes on individual events</h3><ul><li><strong>Nathan's Treasure Hunt</strong> - our best-performing GoD seasonal to date; the reward-ladder structure is the template we now reuse for one-off events.</li><li><strong>Plague Race</strong> - the recurring ranked competition on ZM3D. In Aug 2025 the algorithmically generated levels - everything above level 100 - did not count toward the race, so high-level players could not score (ZOM-459, opened 5 Aug, fixed 25 Aug 2025). It affected scoring for players above level 100, so pre-fix placements and reward settlement in those races are unreliable &mdash; at least one player who was leading lost and had to be compensated by hand. It did not affect revenue; Plague Race carries no IAP.</li><li><strong>Endless Monster Mode</strong> - a permanent ZM3D board mode, not a seasonal event. It unlocks at level 24 and resets daily at 00:00 UTC and weekly on Monday 00:00 UTC, both cron-scheduled in the CDK stack. ZOM-297 was closed on 1 Aug 2025, but that is the ticket close, not the ship: the mode reached players in the release submitted 6 Aug &mdash; Android 0.3.99 on 6 Aug, iOS 0.3.11 on 7 Aug 2025.</li></ul><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"warning\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>2025 weekend live-ops outage.</strong> Domino Delights' weekend events failed to activate, so the published calendar diverged from what players actually saw. QA first reported it on Sunday 29 June 2025 and the events were enabled by hand in the database that day; it recurred unfixed and was reported again on Saturday 12 July. The cause was a scheduler bug &mdash; the generator runs Sunday 00:00 UTC and set the Saturday&ndash;Sunday block to end on that same Sunday, six days before its own start, so the block never activated. Streak Fever was affected from 1 April and Axe Arena from 15 May. A one-line fix was committed on 19 July 2025. <strong>The record contains no deployment of that fix and no message confirming the calendar was healthy again, so this outage has no recorded end</strong> &mdash; do not quote a duration. The lives/energy problem reported in the same thread is a SEPARATE, client-side issue with its own open tickets; it is not part of this outage. Do not backfill or reason about that window from this calendar - the Live-Ops Event Engine page holds the reconstructed timeline and the revenue impact.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Planning cadence</h2><p>As of January 2026, the studio had 7 people (4 paid non-founders and 3 founders), down from a September 2024 peak of 19 - so live-ops planning is deliberately lightweight - one recurring meeting and one shared calendar, not a dedicated ops team. The working rhythm:</p><ul><li><strong>Daily live-ops pod review.</strong> Design, led by Julia Lawson, walks the coming weeks; Frederick Stone participated before his October 2025 departure: which recurring slots fire and whether a one-off drops on top. Company-wide sync is the Friday all-hands.</li><li><strong>There is no technical content lock.</strong> Reward tables are re-imported from Google Sheets hourly in production (<code>IMPORT_REWARDS_SCHEDULE</code> defaults to <code>0 * * * *</code>), so a mid-window sheet edit reaches players within the hour. The 24h season-pass freeze in the Season Pass spec is a process control on top of that, not a mechanism. Windows are cron expressions in the CDK stack and do need a deploy to change.</li><li><strong>Overlapping events are normal.</strong> Domino Delights runs four weekly events concurrently in production, and Zombie Match 3D overlaps Plague Race, Leagues and both Endless Monster resets. Avoiding overlap has been discussed as an aspiration but is not an operating rule.</li><li><strong>Post-event read.</strong> Each event gets a short retro against its target from Product OKRs before the slot is reused.</li></ul><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>The recurring slots (Endless Monster Mode (a permanent board mode with daily and weekly resets, not a seasonal event); Plague Race ranked) are the backbone of the calendar. One-off seasonals like Nathan's Treasure Hunt are layered on for spikes - they are the exception, not the base cadence, and should never displace a recurring slot without documented Product approval.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0038", "message": null, "created_at": "2026-01-31T22:11:24Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/57", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_prod_home", "record": {"id": "ver_4f83e3cd596c4c4c9f203116d8fd5a4a", "page_id": "page_prod_home", "number": 1, "title": "Product & Design Home", "body": "<ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>The <strong>Product &amp; Design</strong> space. GDDs are canonical; targets live in the OKRs; economy changes are reviewed first.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Start here</h2><ul><li><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1\"/><ac:link-body>Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1</ac:link-body></ac:link></li><li><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives &amp; Boosters\"/><ac:link-body>Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives &amp; Boosters</ac:link-body></ac:link></li><li><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link></li></ul>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0016", "message": "Imported", "created_at": "2024-05-04T18:32:24Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/58", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_prod_home", "record": {"id": "ver_6de27527efa57f27bd9fe13760c45d22", "page_id": "page_prod_home", "number": 2, "title": "Product & Design Home", "body": "<ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>The <strong>Product &amp; Design</strong> space. GDDs are canonical; targets live in the OKRs; economy changes are reviewed first.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Start here</h2><ul><li><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1\"/><ac:link-body>Product OKRs - 2025 H1</ac:link-body></ac:link></li><li><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives &amp; Boosters\"/><ac:link-body>Economy Design - Coins, Lives &amp; Boosters</ac:link-body></ac:link></li><li><ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Zombie Match 3D - Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link></li></ul>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0016", "message": null, "created_at": "2025-07-15T12:02:36Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/70", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_season_pass_spec", "record": {"id": "ver_cd3ea56fe48148f4be79a81de36ebb6c", "page_id": "page_season_pass_spec", "number": 1, "title": "ZM3D Season Pass \u2014 Spec", "body": "<p>This is the product spec for the <strong>Zombie Match 3D</strong> <strong>Season Pass</strong> (store title <strong>Puzzles vs Zombies</strong>), written just before launch. The pass is the first paid track on the title and the primary lever we have for lifting ARPU on our existing daily actives. For the core loop, combat layer, and monetization overview this ladders under, see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link>, and for the target it serves see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1\"/><ac:link-body>Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1</ac:link-body></ac:link>.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>At a glance.</strong> Reached production <strong>September 30, 2025</strong> at <strong>$6.99</strong> (one-time unlock per 30-day season). A free track and a premium track run in parallel over a monthly season window, with rewards unlocked by the same live-ops progression players already earn through play.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Goal &amp; positioning</h2><p>We monetize almost entirely through consumables (coins, boosters, extra lives). That caps ARPU because it only reaches players already willing to spend on a fail state. The Season Pass adds a low-friction, predictable monthly product that converts engagement \u2014 not frustration \u2014 into revenue, and gives non-payers a visible reason to log in daily via the free track.</p><ul><li><strong>Cadence</strong> \u2014 one season per calendar month; the track resets and re-themes on the 1st.</li><li><strong>Earn, don't grind</strong> \u2014 pass points come from campaign clears, Endless runs, and daily quests. No separate currency to buy.</li><li><strong>Free track always on</strong> \u2014 every player earns from tier 1; the premium track retro-unlocks all already-earned premium rewards at purchase.</li><li><strong>One pass SKU</strong> \u2014 the monthly Season Pass at $6.99. There is no separate Battle Pass. </li></ul><h2>Reward tracks</h2><p>Each season runs 30 tiers. The free track is deliberately front-loaded so the value of the premium track is legible before a player commits. Premium includes cosmetics and coin/gem sinks plus a material advantage: life capacity increases from 5 to 8.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Tier band</th><th>Free track</th><th>Premium track ($6.99)</th></tr><tr><td>1\u20135</td><td>Coins, 1 booster</td><td>Season avatar frame + coins</td></tr><tr><td>6\u201310</td><td>Extra lives</td><td>Exclusive monster skin</td></tr><tr><td>11\u201320</td><td>Coins</td><td>Booster bundles + gems</td></tr><tr><td>21\u201329</td><td>1 booster</td><td>Coins, gems, tray cosmetic</td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>Coin lump sum</td><td>Signature seasonal skin + gem grant</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Points model</h3><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\"><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[season_pass:\n  price_usd: 6.99          # single monthly SKU\n  tiers: 30\n  points_per_tier: 1000\n  earn:\n    campaign_clear: 100    # points per level cleared\n    endless_per_1000_dmg: 1.0\n    daily_quest: 250\n  window: monthly          # resets on the 1st, re-themes\n  premium_unlock: retroactive]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Rollout</h2><p>Ship to 100% on launch day rather than a slow ramp \u2014 the pass is time-boxed to the month, so a partial rollout would leave early cohorts on a shortened first season. We gate on store approval and a live-ops config freeze the day before.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"note\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Rollout guardrails:</strong></p><ul><li>Do not touch tray count or Endless refill cadence during an active season \u2014 it swings the difficulty curve and skews pass-progression pacing right when we're reading purchase intent.</li><li>Season config (tiers, rewards, theme) is authored in the live-ops tool and locked 24h before the 1st; no hotfixes to reward tables mid-season without Product sign-off.</li><li>Purchase, tier-claim, and daily-active events are tagged for reporting through our attribution and analytics stack so we can read conversion and IAP mix from day one.</li></ul></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>The retained warehouse has no reliable Zombie Match 3D IAP transactions, so the Season Pass share of monthly IAP is unmeasured. Owner: Robert (Product). Design partner: Julia Lawson.</p>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0016", "message": "Imported", "created_at": "2025-10-02T14:40:30Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/71", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_season_pass_spec", "record": {"id": "ver_da119d6feae14baa6d5d36e571b1e3b5", "page_id": "page_season_pass_spec", "number": 2, "title": "ZM3D Season Pass \u2014 Spec", "body": "<p>This is the product spec for the <strong>Zombie Match 3D</strong> <strong>Season Pass</strong> (shipped on the store as <strong>Puzzles vs Zombies</strong> under Calm Play LLC until the transfer to Harmony Games and the rename on 24 July 2025), written just before launch. The pass is the first paid track on the title and the primary lever we have for lifting ARPU on our existing daily actives. For the core loop, combat layer, and monetization overview this ladders under, see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Zombie Match 3D - Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link>, and for the target it serves see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1\"/><ac:link-body>Product OKRs - 2025 H1</ac:link-body></ac:link>.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>At a glance.</strong> Reached production in the week of <strong>September 22-29, 2025</strong> - Android 0.3.127 published Sep 22, iOS 0.3.49 released Sep 29 at <strong>$6.99</strong> (one-time unlock per monthly season). A free track and a premium track run in parallel over the monthly season window, with rewards unlocked by the same live-ops progression players already earn through play.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Goal &amp; positioning</h2><p>We monetize almost entirely through consumables (coins, boosters, extra lives). That caps ARPU because it only reaches players already willing to spend on a fail state. The Season Pass adds a low-friction, predictable monthly product that converts engagement - not frustration - into revenue, and gives non-payers a visible reason to log in daily via the free track.</p><ul><li><strong>Cadence</strong> - production seasons reset monthly on the 1st at 00:00 UTC; the initial launch may be a partial first season.</li><li><strong>Earn, don't grind</strong> - pass points come from campaign clears, Endless runs, and daily quests. No separate currency to buy.</li><li><strong>Level-gated, then always on</strong> - the pass unlocks at player level 30 by default and the unlock level is an active A/B variable. Once unlocked every player earns from tier 1; the premium track retro-unlocks all already-earned premium rewards at purchase.</li><li><strong>One pass SKU</strong> - the monthly Season Pass at $6.99. There is no separate Battle Pass. </li></ul><h2>Reward tracks</h2><p>Each season runs 30 tiers. The free track is deliberately front-loaded so the value of the premium track is legible before a player commits. Premium includes cosmetics and coin/gem sinks plus material advantages - notably raising life capacity from 5 to 8 - alongside booster bundles and gems.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Tier band</th><th>Free track</th><th>Premium track ($6.99)</th></tr><tr><td>1-5</td><td>Coins, 1 booster</td><td>Season avatar frame + coins</td></tr><tr><td>6-10</td><td>Extra lives</td><td>Exclusive monster skin</td></tr><tr><td>11-20</td><td>Coins</td><td>Booster bundles + gems</td></tr><tr><td>21-29</td><td>1 booster</td><td>Coins, gems, tray cosmetic</td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>Coin lump sum</td><td>Signature seasonal skin + gem grant</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Points model</h3><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\"><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[season_pass:\n  price_usd: 6.99          # single monthly SKU\n  tiers: 30\n  points_per_tier: 1000\n  earn:\n    campaign_clear: 100    # points per level cleared\n    endless_per_1000_dmg: 1.0\n    daily_quest: 250\n  window: calendar_month  # resets on the 1st at 00:00 UTC\n  premium_unlock: retroactive]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Rollout</h2><p>Ship to 100% on launch day rather than a slow ramp - the pass is time-boxed to a calendar month, so a partial rollout would leave early cohorts on a shortened first season. We gate on store approval and a live-ops config freeze the day before.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"note\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Rollout guardrails:</strong></p><ul><li>Do not touch tray count or Endless refill cadence during an active season - it swings the difficulty curve and skews pass-progression pacing right when we're reading purchase intent.</li><li>Season config (tiers, rewards, theme) is authored in the live-ops tool and locked 24h before each season opens; no hotfixes to reward tables mid-season without Product sign-off.</li><li>Purchase and tier-claim events are tagged for reporting through our attribution and analytics stack. There is no daily-active read on Zombie Match 3D - the title has no DAU table - so derive volume from installs and retention instead.</li></ul></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>No Season Pass purchase has been recorded: the title's only store-validated sale is a $1.99 bundle on 31 July 2025. Treat season pacing as a design input rather than a revenue lever on this title. Owner: Robert (Product). Design partner: Julia Lawson. Both stayed through the February 2026 wind-down.</p>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0016", "message": null, "created_at": "2026-02-12T14:40:30Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/76", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_zm3d_gdd", "record": {"id": "ver_e221b52d65dc4f89ba1247a346e55863", "page_id": "page_zm3d_gdd", "number": 1, "title": "Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document", "body": "<p>This is the living Game Design Document for <strong>Zombie Match 3D</strong> (store title <strong>Puzzles vs Zombies</strong>). It is the source of truth for the core loop, the RPG combat layer, and monetization. For the coin/life economy see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives &amp; Boosters\"/><ac:link-body>Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives &amp; Boosters</ac:link-body></ac:link>, and for the paid track see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"ZM3D Season Pass \u2014 Spec\"/><ac:link-body>ZM3D Season Pass \u2014 Spec</ac:link-body></ac:link>. This document ladders up to <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1\"/><ac:link-body>Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1</ac:link-body></ac:link>.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>Global launch shipped <strong>May 15</strong>, 2025. This GDD reflects the launch build plus the Season Pass update.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Core mechanic</h2><p>The matcher is a Match-3D collector benchmarked on <em>Match Factory</em>. Objects sit in a physics pile; the player drags items into a <strong>7-slot tray</strong>. Collect any 3 matching objects and they clear from the tray. If all 7 slots fill without a match, it is a blunder: the tray clears and surviving monsters enrage, but play continues. The level is lost only if the resulting damage reduces health to zero. Tray pressure is the primary difficulty dial.</p><ul><li><strong>Pile physics</strong> \u2014 objects settle and occlude each other; digging exposes buried matches.</li><li><strong>7-slot tray</strong> \u2014 a tempo-and-damage penalty, not an automatic fail state; tuning slot count changes felt difficulty more than object count.</li><li><strong>Object families</strong> \u2014 cosmetic skins that map to elemental ammo in the RPG layer.</li></ul><h2>Zombie RPG layer</h2><p>Levels wrap the matcher in combat. Each cleared triple fires the matching element at the current monster. Monsters carry an elemental weakness; hitting the weakness deals bonus damage and can apply a status.</p><h3>Monster / element table</h3><p>The roster is an everyday-people theme rather than classic undead. Minion families scale in tiers; bosses come in standard, Fast and Turbo variants.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Family</th><th>Type</th><th>Tiers</th></tr><tr><td>Punk</td><td>Minion</td><td>1\u20135</td></tr><tr><td>Biker</td><td>Minion</td><td>1\u20134</td></tr><tr><td>Karen</td><td>Minion</td><td>1\u20134</td></tr><tr><td>Afro</td><td>Minion</td><td>1\u20133</td></tr><tr><td>Riot Police, Chef, Scientist, Fire Fighter, Magician, Librarian, Tech Bro, Gym Bro, Baseball Player, Cheerleader</td><td>Minion</td><td>in development</td></tr><tr><td>Weak Boss 180 / Mini Boss 300 / Boss Main 500</td><td>Boss</td><td>standard, Fast, Turbo</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Elemental weaknesses used by boosters and abilities: shock, poison, burn, freeze, splash, stun, blind. Glue is a booster, not an element.</p><h3>Modes</h3><ul><li><strong>Campaign</strong> \u2014 authored levels, escalating monster mixes.</li><li><strong>Endless</strong> \u2014 survival board with an item refill every 30s to keep the pile stocked.</li><li><strong>Infinite-HP Boss</strong> \u2014 a damage-race against a boss whose HP does not deplete to zero; the score is total damage dealt before the tray fills.</li></ul><h2>Monetization</h2><p>The headline product is the <strong>Season Pass</strong> at <strong>$6.99</strong>, reached production September 30, 2025. It runs a free and a premium reward track over a fixed season window; progression is earned through campaign and Endless play. Coin, life, and booster sinks live in the linked Economy doc \u2014 do not duplicate values here.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"note\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Known launch issues (tracked, historical):</strong></p><ul><li>The addressables/font splash stall belongs to Domino Delights (ENG-2346, GoD - Beta, build 0.2.197), not Zombie Match 3D.</li><li>The Zombie Match 3D client has no remote font download.</li></ul></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h3>Boss mode reward config</h3><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\"><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[boss_mode:\n  hp_model: infinite      # score = total damage before tray fill\n  score_to_pass_points:\n    tier_1: 1.0           # Season Pass points per 1000 damage\n    tier_2: 1.5\n  endless_refill_seconds: 30]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>Owner: Robert (Product). Design: Julia Lawson. Changes to tray count or refill cadence must be reviewed against the OKR dashboard before shipping.</p>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0016", "message": "Imported", "created_at": "2025-10-02T08:27:45Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/page_versions/77", "field": "page_id", "value": "page_zm3d_gdd", "record": {"id": "ver_b65180db165e00056b6ba15310c3015c", "page_id": "page_zm3d_gdd", "number": 2, "title": "Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document", "body": "<p>This is the living Game Design Document for <strong>Zombie Match 3D</strong> (shipped on the store as <strong>Puzzles vs Zombies</strong> under Calm Play LLC until the transfer to Harmony Games and the rename on 24 July 2025). It is the source of truth for the core loop, the RPG combat layer, and monetization. For the coin/life economy see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives &amp; Boosters\"/><ac:link-body>Economy Design - Coins, Lives &amp; Boosters</ac:link-body></ac:link>, and for the paid track see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"ZM3D Season Pass \u2014 Spec\"/><ac:link-body>ZM3D Season Pass - Spec</ac:link-body></ac:link>. This document ladders up to <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Product OKRs \u2014 2025 H1\"/><ac:link-body>Product OKRs - 2025 H1</ac:link-body></ac:link>.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>ZM3D never had a global launch. It first became publicly downloadable in the US on Google Play on <strong>April 12, 2025</strong> and on the App Store on <strong>April 18, 2025</strong>; <strong>May 15, 2025</strong> is the day iOS build 1.0.5 went live. This GDD reflects that build plus the Season Pass update.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h2>Core mechanic</h2><p>The matcher is a Match-3D collector benchmarked on <em>Match Factory</em>. Objects sit in a physics pile; the player drags items into a <strong>7-slot tray</strong>. Collect any 3 matching objects and they clear from the tray. If all 7 slots fill without a match it counts as a blunder: the tray clears and surviving monsters enrage, but play continues. It is a tempo penalty, not a fail state - the loss screen only appears at zero health. Tray pressure is the primary difficulty dial.</p><ul><li><strong>Pile physics</strong> - objects settle and occlude each other; digging exposes buried matches.</li><li><strong>7-slot tray</strong> - the primary tempo penalty, not the fail state; tuning slot count changes felt difficulty more than object count.</li><li><strong>Object families</strong> - cosmetic skins that map to elemental ammo in the RPG layer.</li></ul><h2>Zombie RPG layer</h2><p>Levels wrap the matcher in combat. Each cleared triple fires the matching element at the current monster. Monsters carry an elemental weakness; hitting the weakness deals bonus damage and can apply a status.</p><h3>Monster / element table</h3><p>The roster is an everyday-people theme rather than classic undead. Minion families scale in tiers; bosses come in standard, Fast and Turbo variants.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Family</th><th>Type</th><th>Tiers</th></tr><tr><td>Punk</td><td>Minion</td><td>1-5</td></tr><tr><td>Biker</td><td>Minion</td><td>1-4</td></tr><tr><td>Karen</td><td>Minion</td><td>1-4</td></tr><tr><td>Afro</td><td>Minion</td><td>1-3</td></tr><tr><td>Riot Police, Chef, Scientist, Fire Fighter, Magician, Librarian, Tech Bro, Gym Bro, Baseball Player, Cheerleader</td><td>Minion</td><td>in development</td></tr><tr><td>VarC-Mayor1 250 / VarC-Mayor2 225 / VarC-Chef 175 (base HP, scaled at runtime; the older 180/300/500 prefabs are retired)</td><td>Boss</td><td>standard, Fast, Turbo</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Elemental weaknesses used by boosters and abilities: shock, poison, burn, freeze, splash, stun, blind. Glue is a booster, not an element.</p><h3>Modes</h3><ul><li><strong>Campaign</strong> - authored levels, escalating monster mixes.</li><li><strong>Endless</strong> - survival board with an item refill every 30s to keep the pile stocked.</li><li><strong>Infinite-HP Boss</strong> - a damage-race against a boss whose HP does not deplete to zero; the score is total damage dealt before the tray fills.</li></ul><h2>Monetization</h2><p>The headline product is the <strong>Season Pass</strong> at <strong>$6.99</strong>, reached production in the week of September 22-29, 2025. It runs a free and a premium reward track over a fixed season window; progression is earned through campaign and Endless play. Coin, life, and booster sinks live in the linked Economy doc - do not duplicate values here.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"note\"><ac:rich-text-body><p><strong>Known launch issues (tracked, historical):</strong></p><ul><li>Hard crash from consecutive glass-impact SFX/VFX on Android, mostly Samsung (Aug-Sep 2025, ZOM-475), fixed by removing the glass SFX and VFX. The separate addressables splash-hang belongs to Domino Delights.</li><li>The font-download freeze that stalls the splash screen at ~22% on slow connections is also Domino Delights (ENG-2346, May 2025); the ZM3D client has no remote font download.</li></ul></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h3>Boss mode reward config</h3><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\"><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[boss_mode:\n  hp_model: infinite      # score = total damage before tray fill\n  score_to_pass_points:\n    tier_1: 1.0           # Season Pass points per 1000 damage\n    tier_2: 1.5\n  endless_refill_seconds: 30]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>Owner: Robert (Product). Design: Julia Lawson. Both stayed through the February 2026 wind-down. Changes to tray count or refill cadence must be reviewed against the OKR dashboard before shipping.</p>", "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0016", "message": null, "created_at": "2026-02-10T08:27:45Z"}}], "records_checked": 78, "files_selected": 1, "files_completed": 1, "scan_complete": true, "errors": []}}, "files_read_this_call": 1, "sources": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "manifest_sha256": "e6840608051cf49e37aeb94a719fed78e0d38eb902d30f86805b84ea0d67adb6", "freshness": "970c4a92af37d08dd66b69b75daa8db99f043a7078d21e855c130a5f6081383c"}], "scan_complete": true, "persona_filtered": false, "backend": "grouped-record-scan", "scope_note": "Exact direct fields in selected arrays. No SQL is applied. Absence/uniqueness is supported only within complete declared scopes. Manifest hashes are declared provenance, not fresh full-content hashes."}, "checksum": "ba007e680dea097580f1aee176f768be983d192f056da3b2b4192703f31fff14"}